"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[407],{1865:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"get","desc":"Returns the current value at this node.\\n\\nOn the client, tables are read-only proxies unless `clientGuard` is `\\"off\\"`.\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal coins = S.coins.get()\\nlocal stats = S.stats.get()\\n```","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"The value at this node, or `nil` if there is none.","lua_type":"T"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":255,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"snapshot","desc":"Returns a deep copy of this node that you can keep or change without touching the real data.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"A copy of the value.","lua_type":"T"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Tables"],"source":{"line":271,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"set","desc":"Replaces the value at this node. Throws on the client.\\n\\nSetting the root expects a table.\\n\\n```lua\\nS.coins.set(50)\\n```","params":[{"name":"Value","desc":"The new value.","lua_type":"T"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The new value.","lua_type":"T"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":293,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"update","desc":"Replaces the value at this node with the result of a function. Throws on the client.\\n\\n```lua\\nS.coins.update(function(coins)\\n\\treturn coins + 10\\nend)\\n```","params":[{"name":"Updater","desc":"Receives the current value and returns the new one.","lua_type":"(Current: T) -> T"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The new value.","lua_type":"T"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":326,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"mutate","desc":"Changes several fields of a table at once. Strata works out what changed and replicates only that. Throws on the client.\\n\\n```lua\\nS.stats.mutate(function(stats)\\n\\tstats.level += 1\\n\\tstats.xp = 0\\nend)\\n```","params":[{"name":"Mutator","desc":"Receives the table to change in place.","lua_type":"(Target: T) -> ()"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","tags":["Tables"],"source":{"line":345,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"observe","desc":"Calls a function with this node\'s value now and every time it changes.\\n\\nThe listener runs once shortly after you connect, with the current value and a `nil` old value, then on each change with the new and old values. Values that haven\'t changed don\'t fire again.\\n\\nObserving a parent fires when any child changes, and observing a child fires when its parent is replaced. Use [State.changed] if you only want changes.\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal Connection = S.stats.level.observe(function(level, Old)\\n\\tprint(\\"level is\\", level)\\nend)\\n\\nConnection.disconnect()\\n```","params":[{"name":"Listener","desc":"Called with the new value and the old one.","lua_type":"(Value: T, Old: T?) -> ()"}],"returns":[{"desc":"Call `disconnect` on it to stop listening.","lua_type":"Connection"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":372,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"increment","desc":"Adds a number to this node\'s value and returns the new total. A missing\\nvalue counts as `0`. Throws on the client.\\n\\n```lua\\nS.coins.increment(25)\\nS.stats.kills.increment() -- adds 1\\n```","params":[{"name":"By","desc":"How much to add. Defaults to `1`.","lua_type":"number?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The new value.","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":408,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"decrement","desc":"Subtracts a number from this node\'s value and returns the new total.\\nThrows on the client.","params":[{"name":"By","desc":"How much to subtract. Defaults to `1`.","lua_type":"number?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The new value.","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":433,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"toggle","desc":"Flips a boolean and returns the new value. A missing value counts as\\n`false`. Throws on the client.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"The new value.","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":449,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"reset","desc":"Puts this node back to the value it has in your template. On the root\\nit resets everything. Throws on the client, and when the path has no\\ntemplate default (an entry inside an empty map, for example).\\n\\n```lua\\nS.stats.reset()\\n```","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"The new value.","lua_type":"T"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":474,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"fetch","desc":"Returns the server\'s value for this node. On the client it asks the\\nserver and **yields** until the server answers, so it can be trusted for\\nthings like checking a price before showing a purchase. On the server it\\njust reads the value, so shared code can call it anywhere.\\n\\nThrows if the data hasn\'t loaded, the node is `private`, or the client\\nis asking too often. The result is a copy, not a live table.\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal ok, coins = pcall(C.coins.fetch)\\n```","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"The server\'s current value.","lua_type":"T"}],"function_type":"static","yields":true,"source":{"line":505,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"child","desc":"Returns the child node for a key. Works for any key, including ones that\\nshare a name with a node method (a field called `keys`, or `size`).\\n\\n```lua\\nS.items.child(\\"size\\").get()\\n```","params":[{"name":"Key","desc":"The key of the child.","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Node"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":526,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"has","desc":"Returns whether a key exists in this map or array.","params":[{"name":"Key","desc":"The key to look for.","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Maps and arrays"],"source":{"line":541,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"keys","desc":"Returns every key in this map or array.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"{ any }"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Maps and arrays"],"source":{"line":554,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"values","desc":"Returns every value in this map or array.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"{ any }"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Maps and arrays"],"source":{"line":573,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"size","desc":"Returns how many entries this map or array has.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Maps and arrays"],"source":{"line":592,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"clear","desc":"Removes every entry from this map or array. Throws on the client.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","tags":["Maps and arrays"],"source":{"line":610,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"insert","desc":"Sets one key in this map. Throws on the client. Arrays use [State.insertAt] and [State.addNext] instead.\\n\\n```lua\\nS.items.insert(\\"sword_001\\", { damage = 12 })\\n```","params":[{"name":"Key","desc":"The key to set.","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"Value","desc":"The value to store.","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","tags":["Maps and arrays"],"source":{"line":627,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"remove","desc":"Removes one key from this map. Throws on the client.\\n\\nFor **arrays**, pass a string key only if the array is being used as a map.\\nNumeric indices on array-like tables must use [State.removeAt] or\\n[State.removeLast] \u2014 removing by number would leave a gap in the sequence.\\n\\n```lua\\nS.items.remove(\\"sword_001\\") -- map\\nS.inventory.removeAt(2) -- array\\nS.inventory.removeLast() -- array\\n```","params":[{"name":"Key","desc":"The map key to remove (not a numeric array index).","lua_type":"string | any"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The value that was removed, or `nil` if the key was missing.","lua_type":"any"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Maps"],"source":{"line":658,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"addNext","desc":"Adds a value to the end of this array. Throws on the client.","params":[{"name":"Value","desc":"The value to add.","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The new length.","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Arrays"],"source":{"line":683,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"removeLast","desc":"Removes and returns the last value of this array. Throws on the client.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"The removed value, or `nil` if the array is empty.","lua_type":"any"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Arrays"],"source":{"line":699,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"insertAt","desc":"Inserts a value into this array and shifts everything after it. Throws on the client.","params":[{"name":"Index","desc":"The position to insert at.","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"Value","desc":"The value to insert.","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","tags":["Arrays"],"source":{"line":720,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"removeAt","desc":"Removes the value at a position in this array. Throws on the client.","params":[{"name":"Index","desc":"The position to remove.","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"The removed value.","lua_type":"any"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Arrays"],"source":{"line":737,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"isLoaded","desc":"Returns whether this session is still active.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Root only"],"source":{"line":759,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"save","desc":"Saves the session now instead of waiting for the next save. Does nothing on the client.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","tags":["Root only"],"source":{"line":770,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"endSession","desc":"Ends the session. The player is kicked if `kickOnSessionEnd` is on. Does nothing on the client.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","tags":["Root only"],"source":{"line":783,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"replicate","desc":"Sends a full snapshot to the client now. Does nothing on the client.","params":[{"name":"Target","desc":"Who to send to. Defaults to the session owner.","lua_type":"Player?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","tags":["Root only"],"source":{"line":797,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"getSessionInfo","desc":"Returns details about this session.\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal Info = S.getSessionInfo()\\nprint(Info.UserId, Info.LoadedAt, Info.LastSaveAt)\\n```","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"`nil` if the session is not active.","lua_type":"SessionInfo?"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Root only"],"source":{"line":816,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"getMeta","desc":"Reads from the metadata stored beside your data. Metadata is saved with the profile but is not part of your template.","params":[{"name":"MetaKey","desc":"The key to read. Omit it to get a copy of all metadata.","lua_type":"string?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Root only"],"source":{"line":832,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"setMeta","desc":"Writes to the metadata stored beside your data.","params":[{"name":"MetaKey","desc":"The key to write.","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"Value","desc":"The value to store. Must be JSON-compatible.","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","tags":["Root only"],"source":{"line":848,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"getPath","desc":"Returns the path segments from the vault root to this node.\\n\\nUseful when writing generic helpers or logging which field changed.\\n\\n```lua\\nprint(table.concat(S.stats.level.getPath(), \\".\\")) -- \\"stats.level\\"\\n```","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"A shallow copy of the path array. Empty at the root.","lua_type":"{ any }"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Debug"],"source":{"line":870,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"getKey","desc":"Returns the session key this node belongs to (e.g. `\\"Player_123\\"` or an\\nincognito key when that mode is on).","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"string"}],"function_type":"static","tags":["Root only","Debug"],"source":{"line":884,"path":"src/State.luau"}},{"name":"debugDump","desc":"Pretty-prints this node\'s current value (or the whole vault at the root)\\nto the output. Intended for Studio debugging.\\n\\n```lua\\nS.debugDump() -- whole vault\\nS.stats.debugDump() -- just stats\\n```","params":[{"name":"Label","desc":"Optional prefix for the printed line.","lua_type":"string?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","tags":["Debug"],"source":{"line":902,"path":"src/State.luau"}}],"properties":[{"name":"changed","desc":"A signal that fires when this node\'s value changes. Unlike [State.observe]\\nit does not fire for the current value on connect.\\n\\nIt\'s a real object, so it uses method syntax.\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal Connection = S.coins.changed:connect(function(New, Old)\\n\\tprint(New, \\"was\\", Old)\\nend)\\n\\nS.coins.changed:once(function(New) end)\\nlocal New, Old = S.coins.changed:wait()\\n```","lua_type":"Signal","source":{"line":203,"path":"src/State.luau"}}],"types":[],"name":"State","desc":"A typed node for one path in a player\'s data. Every field in your template\\nis a node, and every node has the same few methods. Everything is **dot\\nsyntax**: nodes hand out pre-bound functions, so `S.coins.get()` works with\\nno `self`. The one exception is a node\'s `changed` signal, which is a real\\nobject: `S.coins.changed:connect(fn)`.\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal Data = require(game.ReplicatedStorage.Data).server\\n\\nlocal S = Data:loadVault(Player)\\nif S then\\n\\tS.coins.update(function(coins)\\n\\t\\treturn coins + 50\\n\\tend)\\n\\tS.inventory.addNext(\\"Sword\\")\\n\\n\\t-- Fires once with the current value, then on every change\\n\\tS.coins.observe(function(coins, Old)\\n\\t\\tprint(\\"coins:\\", coins, \\"was\\", Old)\\n\\tend)\\n\\n\\t-- Only on changes\\n\\tlocal Connection = S.coins.changed:connect(function(New, Old)\\n\\t\\tprint(New, \\"was\\", Old)\\n\\tend)\\n\\tConnection.disconnect()\\nend\\n```\\n\\n**All nodes:** `get`, `set`, `update`, `observe`, `changed`\\n**Tables:** `mutate`, `snapshot`\\n**Maps and arrays:** `has`, `keys`, `values`, `size`, `clear`\\n**Maps:** `insert`, `remove`\\n**Arrays:** `addNext`, `removeLast`, `insertAt`, `removeAt`\\n**Root only:** `isLoaded`, `save`, `endSession`, `replicate`, `getSessionInfo`, `getMeta`, `setMeta`\\n\\nWrite methods throw on the client. Change data on the server and let\\nreplication do the rest.\\n\\n:::danger Type solver required\\nAutocomplete needs the new Luau type solver. Runtime works without it.\\n:::","source":{"line":50,"path":"src/State.luau"}}')}}]);